---
import Footer from "@/components/footer.astro";
import Nav from "@/components/nav.astro";
import Base from "@/layouts/base.astro";

const locale = "en";
const title = "Privacy policy | AwesomeWorks";
const description =
  "How AwesomeWorks processes personal data from the contact form on awesomeworks.ai: controller, purposes, recipients, retention periods, and GDPR rights.";
---

<Base title={title} description={description} locale={locale}>
  <Nav locale={locale} minimal={true} altPath="/pl/prywatnosc/" />
  <main class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 pb-20 pt-28 md:pt-32">
    <p class="font-mono text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-primary">Data protection</p>
    <h1 class="mt-4 text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-white md:text-4xl">Privacy policy</h1>
    <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-white/65">Effective from September 6, 2026</p>

    <div class="mt-8 border border-primary/35 bg-[var(--surface)] p-6">
      <p class="text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-white">
        <strong>Data controller:</strong> Awesome Works AI Rafał Łazicki (sole proprietorship), VAT ID PL5223202536,
        Warsaw, Poland (“AwesomeWorks”, “we”).
      </p>
      <p class="mt-3 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-white">
        <strong>Contact for data matters:</strong>
        <a href="mailto:hello@awesomeworks.ai" class="font-semibold underline decoration-primary/40 underline-offset-2 hover:text-primary">hello@awesomeworks.ai</a>
      </p>
    </div>

    <section class="mt-10">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold tracking-tight text-white">1. What data we process</h2>
      <ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-2 pl-5 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-white/65">
        <li>
          <strong class="text-white">Contact form:</strong> full name, company name (optional), phone number, email
          address, and message content, plus the device's IP address (used to enforce anti-abuse limits).
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong class="text-white">Technical site data:</strong> standard hosting server logs (including IP address
          and browser type), necessary to serve the site and keep it secure.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong class="text-white">Correspondence:</strong> data you provide when writing to us directly at
          hello@awesomeworks.ai.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-10">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold tracking-tight text-white">2. Purposes and legal bases</h2>
      <ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-2 pl-5 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-white/65">
        <li>Handling your inquiry and getting back to you: art. 6(1)(b) GDPR (pre-contractual steps) and art. 6(1)(f) (legitimate interest).</li>
        <li>Site security and abuse prevention (including form submission limits): art. 6(1)(f) GDPR.</li>
        <li>Establishing or defending legal claims: art. 6(1)(f) GDPR.</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="mt-3 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-white/65">
        Providing your data in the form is voluntary, but without your name, phone number, and email address we will
        not be able to respond to the inquiry.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-10">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold tracking-tight text-white">3. What happens to the form data</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-white/65">
        A form submission goes to our backend hosted on Hetzner Online GmbH servers (data center in Germany, EU).
        There we store it as an inquiry in CallWise, our own contact-handling system (infrastructure also in the EU),
        and the team gets an email notification sent through the Resend service. We do not sell form data and do not
        use it for marketing without your consent.
      </p>
      <ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-2 pl-5 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-white/65">
        <li><strong class="text-white">Hetzner Online GmbH</strong> (Germany, EU): backend and database hosting.</li>
        <li><strong class="text-white">CallWise</strong>: our own system where inquiries are handled (EU infrastructure).</li>
        <li><strong class="text-white">Resend</strong> (USA): email notification about the inquiry; transfers outside the EEA are secured with Standard Contractual Clauses (SCC).</li>
        <li><strong class="text-white">GitHub, Inc.</strong> (USA): static site hosting (GitHub Pages) and its technical logs; transfers outside the EEA secured with SCC.</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="mt-3 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-white/65">
        Data may also be disclosed to entities authorized under applicable law.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-10">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold tracking-tight text-white">4. How long we keep the data</h2>
      <ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-2 pl-5 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-white/65">
        <li><strong class="text-white">Inquiry data</strong>: for the time needed to handle the inquiry and any resulting cooperation, then until the limitation period for claims expires.</li>
        <li><strong class="text-white">IP address used for rate limits</strong>: up to 30 days.</li>
        <li><strong class="text-white">Technical logs</strong>: according to the hosting provider's settings.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-10">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold tracking-tight text-white">5. Your rights</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-white/65">
        You have the right to: access your data, rectify it, erase it, restrict processing, data portability, and to
        object to processing based on legitimate interest. Send requests to hello@awesomeworks.ai. You also have the
        right to lodge a complaint with the President of the Polish Personal Data Protection Office (PUODO),
        ul. Stawki 2, 00-193 Warsaw, Poland.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-10">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold tracking-tight text-white">6. Cookies and browser storage</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-white/65">
        The site uses no analytics or marketing cookies. In your browser's storage (localStorage, sessionStorage) we
        keep only the demo chat window's settings, such as the conversation history for the current tab. This data
        never leaves your browser and does not reach us.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-10">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold tracking-tight text-white">7. Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-white/65">
        We may update this policy, for example when the scope of services or the list of providers changes. The
        current version, with its effective date, is always published on this page.
      </p>
    </section>
  </main>
  <Footer locale={locale} />
</Base>
